{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794176435,"nonce":"w/mPjrFVmpOb2KM07+5xkfxm8uo=","title":"issue list is slow where many issues share a Jira key and display.id is jira","message":"Measured after b62203b6 in a Jira-bound clone with display.id=jira: about 1k live issues, 2k issue refs and a 12k-line packed-refs file (many copies per Jira key). `git work issue list length` takes 5.8s (7.0s user, 2.1s sys).\n\nLikely cause, not yet profiled: building the human-id index (cache/display.go, drawnAliases -\u003e aliasNamed -\u003e reachAll) loads every copy of a shared alias from disk through dag.Read, and go-git's packed-ref lookup scans packed-refs linearly for each ref. Possible directions: keep each copy's reach on the excerpt so the index loads no entity, or resolve the refs in one pass.\n\nStart from a SIGQUIT or pprof profile of the slow run; the clone that showed it can supply one.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["core"],"parent":"fd6c808e0edecb1a7b12ddc7d2675160c444c5698b359d5d92a49b650b5316d0","status":"backlog","type":"task"}}]}